bug_descriptions |bug_id, line_num, content|
    web_render_af_latin_port_wall_clock_ab_owed_2026-11-28, 0, "Owed measurement, not a defect: the Latin autohinter port (src/lib/common/encoding/sfnt_af_latin.spl) was accepted on interpreter dispatch counts because the box ran at load 20 to 30 and a wall-clock A/B could not resolve 2 percent (same page 3.2, 6.7 and 9.6 CPU-seconds in three rounds on both sides). Counts, SIMPLE_INTERP_PROFILE=1, whole 1x render, head against base 3cb5a3d3eeb: html 223,697,890 -> 224,324,954 (+0.28 percent), css-paint 350,726,239 -> 351,168,972 (+0.13 percent). Outline build about 3.0 ms against 2.5 to 2.9 ms on the base, 40 to 139 builds a catalog page."
    web_render_af_latin_port_wall_clock_ab_owed_2026-11-28, 1, "To do in a quiet window: the alternating wall-clock A/B on the eight 1x catalog pages, lane head against its base, at least 3 rounds with the first side alternated, medians, binary identity recorded; limit 2 percent. Close with the numbers; if a page exceeds the limit, the per-glyph analysis that does not depend on the size (directions, weak points, segments, links) can be cached per glyph."

